    "confidence": 0.92,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02724 is refunded in full to the rider, and no compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver did arrive at the pin and wait. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02724) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 21:23:45 to 21:27:05 — a continuous, qualifying dwell of 200 seconds across 21 fixes — and the trip record's own 'arrived' event (EV-TRIP-02724, 21:23:45) matches the first in-geofence fix. So POL-NS-01 limbs (a), (b) and (c) hold: the 200-second dwell exceeds the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), and the arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 — at 21:23:45 the driver was stationary essentially at the pin (0.11 m from it), so neither POL-NS-05 trigger (over 300 m away, or 15 km/h or more) is present.\n\nWhy the fee fails anyway. The trip was terminated by the driver under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01(d) says in terms that this code does not satisfy the limb: it is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider, and it is not RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. Because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, POL-NS-01 fixes the outcome itself — the fee is not chargeable, the rider is refunded in full, no driver compensation is payable, and the mis-selected reason code goes into referrals as a driver-education item. POL-NS-04 reaches the same result independently: the rider sent a coordinating message ('at the lift lobby', 21:24:45), the driver neither replied nor placed an in-app call in the 143 seconds before cancelling at 21:27:08, and the rider's device was within 17.7 m of the pin across all 43 of her fixes — well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius.\n\nAmount. The cancellation-fee line of EV-FARE-02724 is SGD 4.50 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and it reconciles with the platform_policy figure of 4.50, so no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect arises. The full SGD 4.50 is refunded; the refund is the cancellation-fee line only, as no booking or platform fee was charged on this cancelled trip. Driver compensation is nil.\n\nClaims addressed. Driver side: the arrival, limb-(a), dwell, no-false-marker, rider-presence, fare-reconciliation and no-escalation claims are accepted — but they establish only that the driver was at the pin, which is precisely the state that triggers the DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE branch against the fee. The claim that SGD 3.60 compensation is payable under POL-NS-07 is rejected: POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (d) fails. Rider side: the limb-(d) claim is accepted and is decisive, and the refund-amount claim is accepted. The two POL-NS-06 shortfall claims are rejected on the arithmetic — the dwell was 200 seconds against a 180-second minimum, a 20-second surplus, not a shortfall (the negative shortfall_sec of -20.0 records surplus, not deficit), so POL-NS-06 is not engaged. The rider's anti-farming point is accepted but adds nothing.\n\nImpairment and confidence. EV-ADVIS-02724-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); nothing in this ruling rests on it — the single continuous run clears the minimum without any accumulation across intervals — so its absence changes neither the outcome nor the confidence cap. The claims citing it were discarded for failing to disclose the impairment. The deciding facts — the DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE reason code (EV-TRIP-02724, weight 1.0) and the driver's in-radius position (EV-GPS-02724, weight 1.0) — are carried by full-weight artifacts, so no POL-GEN-02 discount applies and confidence sits at 0.92. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: no admissible artifacts contradict each other, the repeat-pairing and abuse counters are zero, the anti-farming check does not trip, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue."
  },
