    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-01 — driver education: this trip was terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which POL-NS-01(d) expressly excludes from the chargeable no-show reason codes (RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE, EXCESSIVE_WAIT). Review the reason-code selection with driver DRV-09724."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the contested charge was SGD 4.50, the cancellation fee shown on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02724, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). It is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four conditions hold. Three do. Limb (a): the trip record (EV-TRIP-02724) carries a driver 'arrived' event at 21:23:45. Limb (b): the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02724) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from the first qualifying fix at 21:23:45, matching that event to the second with no clock skew (POL-NS-08(a) not engaged). Limb (c): the driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous 200 seconds, 21:23:45 to 21:27:05, which meets the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). Limb (d) fails. The trip was terminated under cancellation_reason_code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01(d) states expressly that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE does not satisfy limb (d) — it is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider, which his statement to the platform confirms. Because the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius (closest fix 0.11 m from the pin), POL-NS-01 fixes the outcome for that case: the fee is not chargeable, it is refunded in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe rider is also exonerated on her own conduct. Under POL-NS-04 she sent a coordinating message at 21:24:45 ('at the lift lobby'); the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds and made no in-app call before cancelling at 21:27:08 (EV-CHAT-02724; trip_record.in_app_calls empty); and her device trace (EV-GPS-02724) places her within the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius for all 43 of her qualifying fixes (mean 13.8 m, max 17.7 m). This route also gives a full refund with no driver compensation, so the outcome is the same on either ground.\n\nThe driver's claims are accepted but do not change the result. His points that the arrival marker was true (POL-NS-05 not triggered: minimum distance 0.11 m, no 15 kph motion), that the dwell exceeded the free waiting period, that the arrival and GPS clocks agree, and that his profile shows no fee-farming pattern (no_show_terminations_30d = 1 of 120 completed trips = 0.008, far below the 0.08 limb) are all correct on the evidence. They cannot carry the fee, because limb (d) fails independently. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; it is not, so no compensation is payable. The figure would have been SGD 3.60 (80 percent of SGD 4.50) and is not paid.\n\nThe rider's shortfall argument is rejected on arithmetic. The claim that the 200-second dwell was '20 seconds short' of the 180-second waiting period is the wrong way round: 200 seconds is 20 seconds more than 180, and the derived shortfall is −20 seconds. POL-NS-06 (premature cancellation / waiting-period shortfall) is therefore not engaged, and the refund does not depend on it.\n\nThe traffic-advisory claims filed by both sides were discarded at the citation check because they cited the MISSING advisory EV-ADVIS-02724-01 without disclosing its issue code (MISSING_ARTIFACT). Nothing turns on that artifact either way: limb (i) accumulation is not needed, because the single 200-second run already clears the 180-second minimum.\n\nEvidence weight and routing. Every artifact relied on carries weight_multiplier 1.0, and no policy-level impairment fires under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (no clock skew, no trace gap or short sample, rider track present, chat message count matches, fare line reconciles to the SGD 4.50 figure in force). Confidence is therefore not discounted: 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation arises. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue, subject to appeal."
  },
